    "summary": "A document a chat turn presents for approval is opened in the review pane. New module vscode-plugin/src/chat/review-presenter.ts (createReviewPresenter: begin() returns a per-turn handle with toolResult(output) and end()): a tool result carrying pendingApproval.artifactPath opens the pending document with that path at once; the turn's end opens every document that became pending during the turn and was not opened in it; a turn begun while the one before has not ended carries that turn's state on, and the earlier turn's end opens nothing. The chat host (chat-panel.ts) begins a presented turn just before turns.start, passes each non-error tool result from the run sink, and ends it in a finally around the awaited run; a followed turn begins one lazily on its first event and ends it when the follow ended. Each call is wrapped so a throwing presenter is logged. The review client gains pendingDocuments(); the review host's openArtifact gains quiet, createPanel gains opts.quiet (Beside with preserveFocus in extension.ts, Active otherwise) and the channel's reveal gains an optional preserveFocus; vscode.d.ts declares the two forms. review-wiring.test.ts's two assertions on the createPanel source are restated. Tests: ten, one per subject of the design. Mutations of the presenter, the call sites and the quiet open each failed the tests after two tests were tightened. One deviation worth stating: the start list is requested synchronously inside begin() so it is the list of that moment. The design's unverified point (a brainstorm SPEC's path) was not checked in this build; such a document is still opened by the end-of-turn rule.",
    "testRecord": {
      "md": "docs/standalone/open-document-presented-approval-review-pane-E20261013e62a9269/S001/TESTS.md"
    },
